VK-AMPS Control — Enhancements & Bug Fixes (0.34beta - current)

Added a "Peak hold" checkbox to the main dashboard (Peak card, all three view modes). Unchecked, the Peak number tracks the live output in real time instead of holding the highest reading since the last transmission; the existing Setup "Peak Hold Duration" slider still governs the held-mode timeout. Preference persists and travels with exported/imported settings.
Bugfixes

Setup dialog now opens at a comfortable size in Compact too, not just Vertical (commit 09f5494) — previously it could render squeezed into Compact's small locked window, same problem Vertical already had fixed.
Fixed the new Peak hold checkbox misaligning Peak's number against VSWR's in Compact/Expert (a side effect of the checkbox's first placement).
Fixed a related Expert-mode regression where that same misalignment fix made the Peak card grow, which — because Forward Power's height derives from Peak/VSWR's row in the grid layout — grew the whole window's required height and left spurious scrollbars on an already-open window.
-----------------




(0.33beta)

Enhancement

Vertical view: the Operate/Bypass pill is now always visible in the status row next to ON AIR (previously tucked behind the "⋮" menu) — swapped places with the LINK pill, which moved into that "⋮" menu instead. Reasoning: Operate is the more consequential control day-to-day (whether the amp will actually amplify right now), so it shouldn't require an extra click to reach.


(0.32)

*** Enhancements ***

New Vertical dashboard layout — a third view mode alongside Compact/Expert for docking down one side of a screen; later redesigned to match a minimalist reference mockup (always-visible ON AIR/LINK status row, single-line Peak/VSWR, seamless Reflected/Drive/Current card, unified Voltage/Temp card, thinner Forward Power bar).
Compact/Vertical/Expert selector collapsed into a single "View Mode" dropdown, replacing the three-button topbar toggle to cut clutter.
Expert view reorganized — Antenna's port buttons and the voltage-rail choice (Low ~41V / High ~58V) folded into the Forward Power card as a 2×2 grid with Temp/Voltage (Temp on top, voltage-rail choice beside Temp, Antenna beside Voltage), freeing the sidebar for a bigger Power History chart. Antenna's old standalone card/pop-out was retired as part of the move. Rail buttons now read "Voltage Low"/"Voltage High" and are sized to match the Temp tile.
Mini-HUD/Setup buttons show real text labels ("Mini-HUD", "Setup") instead of bare icons once relocated into the Vertical view's overflow menu, matching the other listed items there.


*** Bug Fixes *** 

Fixed Compact's close button getting clipped off-window when the connection state was RECONNECTING (the widest status string, which the window hadn't reserved room for).
Fixed Vertical's Current tile getting clipped off the bottom of the window on 1080p screens; tightened overall height.
Fixed Vertical's antenna buttons not actually filling their row (a flex-parent sizing bug left them bunched left with dead space).
Fixed the window staying oversized after switching Vertical → Compact via the View Mode dropdown — traced to a one-frame race only reproducible through a real (not synthetic) <select> interaction.
Fixed Mini-HUD's popup showing a dead gap when opened while Vertical was active (a CSS rule meant only for the main dashboard was leaking into the popped-out panel).
Fixed spurious scrollbars appearing in Expert view from an exact-pixel-boundary auto-fit, and a collapsed/garbled Power History chart axis when no data had loaded yet.
Fixed Power History leaving a dead-space gap below the chart in Expert view (tried stretching to match the sidebar first; that just relocated the gap, so the chart's own minimum height was raised instead).
Also: ON AIR/live-meter debounce decoupled from Peak Hold Duration and lowered to 1s for faster clearing after a real TX stop (direct tradeoff against the amp's own tx-flag flicker risk).



0.18beta → 0.20beta (current)

Bug Fixes
Fixed Voltage/Temp tiles wrapping and misalignment in Compact view — the "V" unit was wrapping onto its own line, and the label/value weren't centered together. Both fixed and verified against the real running app.
Fixed a multi-second delay in the power meter after stopping and restarting TX. This took several rounds to fully run down:
Telemetry now re-registers immediately the instant a fresh transmission is detected, instead of waiting on a slow independent timer.
Found and fixed the real bottleneck: the app was only checking the amp's status once every 15 seconds during idle gaps, so a restart could go unnoticed for up to 15s. Dropped to 1 second.
Hardened the telemetry retrigger against packet loss on lossy links (VPNs in particular) — bursts a few quick resends instead of one, and tightened socket timing that was silently adding up to 0.5s of its own delay.
Final root-cause fix, based on direct video comparison against another independent app: the periodic telemetry refresh interval was still too conservative. Dropped from 1.5s down to 0.3s, closing the gap much further.
Fixed the "ON AIR stuck" display bug. ON AIR was actually clearing correctly, but the Peak/VSWR/Reflected/Drive/Current readings were staying non-zero for however long the Peak Hold Duration slider was set to — sometimes up to 60 seconds — making it look like the amp was still transmitting. The live readings now always clear in lockstep with ON AIR, completely independent of the Peak Hold slider; only the Peak number itself still respects that slider, since that's what it's actually for.

** Enhancements / Adjustments
Reduced the default/minimum Peak Hold Duration twice by direct request: 17s → 10s → 5s.


0.18beta Release Notes (Latest - ping me for the binaries)
Bug Fixes

Fixed Compact view forcing a ~20px dead-space gap at the bottom of the window. The window's minimum-height floor was set slightly above Compact's actual content height, so the window could never shrink all the way to fit — now it locks to its true content size with no forced gap.
Fixed a startup error where the app's screen-height detection silently failed on every launch (a pywebview API change), causing "fit to content" windows to fall back to an oversized guess instead of the real screen size.
Enhancements

Tightened remaining Compact-view spacing: reduced side padding and bottom margins further now that the window fits its content exactly, for a noticeably more compact layout.
Removed the redundant "VK3AMP" text label from the topbar — the logo already displays the name, so the separate heading was unnecessary duplication. The "Handcrafted in Australia" tagline and version number remain.
All three layout/spacing fixes were verified live against the real running app (via WebView2 remote debugging) before shipping, confirming no regressions in wrapping, overflow, or window sizing.


0.17beta
Enhancements

Hardened the TCP/UDP transport: OS-level TCP keepalive to catch a silently dropped connection faster, exponential backoff on repeated UDP telemetry failures (was retrying every 1s forever), and UDP telemetry now verifies it's actually the amp sending the data before displaying it.
Added rolling p50/p95 logging for command-confirm round-trip time and telemetry frame cadence, to support future tuning decisions with real numbers instead of guesses.
Changed

Removed the bundled Npcap driver installer. Cold connects lose the broadcast-ARP latency fix it enabled (falls back to the slower default ARP path, ~15-18s worst case) but the installer no longer silently installs a third-party network driver.
0.16beta
Enhancements

Compact view redesigned: Reflected/Drive/Current moved into the Forward Power card as compact mini-gauges, antenna buttons relocated into the same row, and the window now locks to an exact-fit size instead of leaving dead space from a stale saved geometry.
Topbar now follows the selected theme (light/dark/colorblind/high-contrast) instead of always rendering as a fixed dark bar.
First-run Setup dialog's serial connection field replaced with a detected-COM-ports dropdown (plus rescan), instead of typing a port name blind.
Added Report a Bug / Request a Feature buttons under Setup > Diagnostics, pre-filled with app version and connection type.
Trimmed scapy's import cost in the startup ARP-priming path (~180ms faster app launch, measured).
Bug Fixes

Fixed Compact-view text clipping/squeezing at text-scale settings above the default (antenna/band label and meter value boxes).
Fixed inconsistent lowercase "w" units on Reflected/Drive tiles.
Fixed a CSS comment accidentally closed early by its own content, which had been silently dropping the entire light-theme variable block.
Fixed three hover states that were invisible against the new light-theme topbar.
Fixed compiler.iss having a hardcoded developer-machine path, which made the installer fail to build on any other machine.
0.15beta
Enhancements

Reduced redundant JSON encoding in the WebSocket broadcast path (status/telemetry events were being encoded twice per event, then re-encoded again per connected client) - fewer encode passes on the hot path that fires on every status reply and multiple times per second during TX.
Bug Fixes

Fixed a live telemetry timestamp mismatch: the value shown live and the value later replayed from history could disagree because each encoding pass independently sampled the clock.
Hardened WINUSB cleanup on a failed connect (removed a redundant/riskier interface-release call that could mask the real error) and fixed a Windows build incorrectly checking for a Linux-only timeout error code.
